  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Test labels use first-rollout lengths capped at M = 2,048 tokens; the prefill-only readout does not condition on decoding-time parameters (temperature, top-k), and capped completions enter RLS at their served <= 2,048 length without revealing uncapped latent lengths.",
    "RLS uses uniform equal weights across all incorporated completions with no forgetting factor or sliding window (Appendix A.2); updates require full q = 8 completion batches (incomplete final batches drop at shutdown), leaving pending requests on M or stale theta_pub until transfer and publication finish.",
    "The 30,569x parameter reduction counts only static readout weights (16.39 KB), excluding the ~64 MiB FP32 inverse precision matrix P (O(d^2)), O(Nd) cached active features, O(qd^2 + q^2d + q^3) FP64 solver updates, and PCIe D2H traffic.",
    "Shortest-first scheduling trades tail fairness for mean latency: LEAP, LEAP+RLS, and TIE keep higher P95 response time than FCFS, and RLS raises P95 on MATH (Table 4).",
    "Prototype integration covers single-A800 vLLM 0.8.5.post1 V0 eager mode only; multi-GPU parallelism, prefix caching, and chunked prefill are not tested and alter prefill overlap slack.",
    "Table 2 (-S vs. -D) uses repeated-generation vs. round-0 remaining-length targets; Table 3 and Figure 6 are single-run host observations (with a concurrent job on GPU 1 and cores 12-15 at 60/80/100 req/s in Fig. 6); Table 4 replay excludes predictor runtime overhead."
  ],
